<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" target="china_maritime_pressure::militarization_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Faster compute growth among rival actors enables more capable maritime ISR, autonomy and targeting systems that China perceives as an operational threat, prompting increased naval patrols, deployments and force posture in adjacent seas.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">china_maritime_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" target="china_maritime_pressure::supply_concentration" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid increases in demand for high-end accelerators and leading-node wafers concentrate production in a small set of specialized fabs and suppliers (e.g., Taiwan, S. Korea), increasing geographic concentration of critical supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">china_maritime_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" target="hormuz_standoff::geo_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid increases in available AI compute accelerate development and fielding of maritime surveillance, targeting and autonomous strike systems that prompt reciprocal force deployments, warnings and diplomatic escalation around the Strait.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" target="hormuz_standoff::maritime_incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded compute enables more effective AI-enabled cyber and autonomy tools (AIS spoofing, automated targeting, swarming drones) that increase the frequency of navigation disruptions, interdictions and kinetic skirmishes in the Strait.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Faster expansion of aggregate compute enables quicker training and dissemination of advanced perception, guidance and swarm-control models that are repurposed for weaponized drones, increasing their operational autonomy, sortie rates and lethality on the battlefield.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::compute_capacity_growth" target="russia_ukraine_war::maritime_attack_intensit" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater available compute accelerates development of autonomous surface and sub-surface vehicle control and mine-detection/avoidance countermeasures, which adversaries adopt to mount more frequent and effective small-boat, mine and unmanned-naval attacks against shipping and ports.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
