<edge source="china_maritime_pressure::supply_concentration" target="global_monetary_stress::monetary_policy_tightnes" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharper geographic concentration of critical supply chains increases the probability and magnitude of supply disruptions that translate quickly into upward consumer and producer price pressures, compelling central banks to tighten policy to contain inflation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_maritime_pressure</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_maritime_pressure::supply_concentration" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::financial_integration" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater geographic concentration of critical hardware and component supply chains raises operational and geopolitical risk on AI revenue streams, making banks and capital markets less willing to securitize or embed those assets into integrated financial instruments.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">china_maritime_pressure</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
