<edge source="global_monetary_stress::intervention_intensity" target="china_maritime_pressure::semiconductor_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained large-scale FX and asset-market interventions consume foreign-currency reserves and constrain import financing for high-value capex (tools, EUV-equipment), causing delays or cancellations of fab upgrades and thereby slowing growth in operational semiconductor capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">china_maritime_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::intervention_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large, persistent public FX interventions (e.g., by the Russian central bank defending the ruble) rapidly draw down FX reserves and hard‑currency liquidity, constraining imports of precision components and fuel logistics that sustain high-frequency drone strike operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::intervention_intensity" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_infra_financing_flow" id="0">
