<edge source="global_monetary_stress::safe_haven_flow" target="china_maritime_pressure::trade_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Surges into safe-haven assets (USD/Treasuries) tighten dollar liquidity and push up global borrowing costs for dollar‑invoiced maritime trade, raising working-capital pressures that reduce short-term seaborne trade volumes.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">china_maritime_pressure</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::safe_haven_flow" target="hormuz_standoff::geo_tension_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in safe-haven flows (flight into USD/Treasuries) strengthens the dollar and tightens external financing for Gulf states, increasing economic pressure on those governments and prompting more aggressive diplomatic and military posturing around the Strait.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::safe_haven_flow" target="russia_ukraine_war::escalation_perception" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Abrupt surges into safe-haven assets drive wider EM funding spreads and market volatility that policymakers and market participants interpret as heightened systemic stress, raising the subjective expectation that localized conflict (e.g., Russia–Ukraine) could escalate or spill over.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_stress::safe_haven_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::financial_integration" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in safe‑haven demand reallocates institutional capital into liquid government assets and away from illiquid, securitized or structured AI‑related instruments, directly reducing the pace of financial integration of AI assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_monetary_stress</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
